<% const title = 'Email'; %>
<h1>Email</h1>
<p class="muted">Connects the office Microsoft 365 mailbox so driver applications and DOT packages notify the office by email. Sends through Microsoft Graph with an OAuth2 application permission — no mailbox password involved, and it works even when the tenant blocks plain-password SMTP.</p>
<% if (ok) { %><div class="alert ok"><%= ok %></div><% } %>
<% if (err) { %><div class="alert err"><%= err %></div><% } %>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0">Status</h2>
  <% if (!envOk) { %>
    <p><strong>Not set up yet.</strong> The server needs the Microsoft app credentials first. In the Microsoft Entra admin center:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Identity → Applications → App registrations → New registration.</strong> Name it <code>Fuel Ledger Mail</code>, single tenant. (No redirect URI needed.)</li>
      <li><strong>API permissions → Add a permission → Microsoft Graph → Application permissions</strong> → check <strong>Mail.Send</strong> → Add permissions, then <strong>Grant admin consent</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Certificates &amp; secrets → New client secret</strong> → copy the secret <strong>value</strong> (not the ID). Also copy the <strong>Application (client) ID</strong> and <strong>Directory (tenant) ID</strong> from the app's Overview page.</li>
      <li>On Render (service → Environment), set <code>MS_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>MS_TENANT_ID</code> and <code>MS_CLIENT_SECRET</code> to those three values, then come back here and send a test.</li>
    </ol>
  <% } else { %>
    <p><strong>Ready ✓</strong> — the app authenticates to Microsoft 365 as itself and sends as the office mailbox via Microsoft Graph.</p>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/email/test">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
      <button class="btn-primary" type="submit">Send test email</button>
    </form>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/email/check" style="margin-top:.5rem">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
      <button class="btn" type="submit">Check Microsoft permissions</button>
    </form>
    <% if (notifyEmail) { %><p class="muted">Test and form notifications go to <code><%= notifyEmail %></code>.</p><% } %>
  <% } %>
  <p class="muted">Sending method in use: <strong><%= mode === 'oauth' ? 'Microsoft Graph (OAuth2)' : mode === 'smtp' ? 'SMTP username/password' : 'none configured' %></strong>. Notifications are always saved to the database even if email fails.</p>
</div>
